  "body": "The previous definition of fully exit fullscreen could unfullscreen\nelements in top layer synchronously. If those elements were iframes,\nthe contentDocument would get handled in a following animation frame\ntask, leaving everything in an odd state in the interim.\n\nExposing the concept of fully exiting to scripts is https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/70.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n[Preview](https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/branch-snapshots/fully-exit-fullscreen/) | [Diff](https://s3.amazonaws.com/pr-preview/whatwg/fullscreen/cbdc4f7...9330439.html)",
